    "id": "c82be6059b1fc8e623781b3d",
    "path": "arrow_avro::writer::format::AvroBinaryFormat",
    "name": "AvroBinaryFormat",
    "owner": null,
    "crate": "arrow-avro",
    "version": "59.3.0",
    "kind": "struct",
    "signature": "struct AvroBinaryFormat",
    "docs": "Unframed Avro binary streaming format (\"raw Avro record body bytes (no prefix, no OCF header)\").\n\nEach record written by the stream writer contains only the raw Avro\nrecord body bytes (i.e., the Avro binary encoding of the datum) with **no**\nper-record prefix and **no** Object Container File (OCF) header.\n\nThis format is useful when another transport provides framing (for example,\nlength-delimited buffers) or when embedding Avro record payloads inside a\nlarger envelope.",
